<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alborz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Alborz is a mountain range in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, running along the southern side of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>. Its fortresses, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alamut">Alamut</a>, became strongholds of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismaili-state">Nizari Ismailis</a> after their split from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>. It is mentioned in the Fatimid profile as the base of this breakaway <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> tradition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alborz.jpg" alt="Alborz" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hansueli Krapf · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_View_of_Damavand_26.11.2008_04-23-59.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
